<!-- SYNTHETIC FIXTURE: NEGATIVE TWIN of synth-ubl-good-not-subject_ubl.xml.
     Byte-for-byte identical to that clean not-subject-to-VAT (category O)
     invoice EXCEPT a VAT-scheme Seller PartyTaxScheme/CompanyID (BT-31,
     DE000000000) is ADDED back to the Seller party.

     Category O is the ODD ONE OUT: its BR-O-02 is a PROHIBITION, the inverse
     polarity of every other family's -02 requirement. An Invoice carrying a
     'Not subject to VAT' (O) invoice line SHALL NOT contain a Seller VAT
     identifier (BT-31), a Seller tax representative VAT id (BT-63) or a Buyer
     VAT identifier (BT-48). Re-introducing the Seller VAT id therefore makes
     BR-O-02 fire — and it is the ONLY fired rule. Everything else is intact:
     the O lines still carry no line VAT rate (BR-O-05), the single O breakdown
     still has BT-119 = 0 (BR-DE-14), tax = 0.00 (BR-O-09), the mandated
     VATEX-EU-O exemption reason (BR-O-10) and O-only exclusivity
     (BR-O-11/12/13/14), and the arithmetic is untouched (VAT total 0.00, tax
     inclusive = tax exclusive = 7500.00 all still reconcile). Adding a Seller
     VAT id does NOT trip BR-DE-16 (O is not in its S/Z/E/AE/K/G/L/M trigger
     set) and its DE000000000 value is format-clean, so no other rule fires.
     Exactly one distinct fatal, isolating the BR-O-02 prohibition shape:
     valid=false, exit 1. -->
